@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{copilot-extras.el} extends the @samp{copilot.el} package@comma{} which
integrates GitHub Copilot into Emacs.  The stock @samp{copilot-mode} is a
simple on/off toggle with no built-in awareness of buffer context.
This extension adds two pieces of missing functionality:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Conditional activation}: enable Copilot automatically in
programming buffers while skipping read-only buffers and
user-specified modes (@ref{Conditional activation, , Conditional activation}).
@item
@strong{Restart workaround}: quickly cycle @samp{copilot-mode} off and on when
the process stops responding (@ref{Restarting Copilot, , Restarting Copilot}).
@item
@strong{Noise suppression}: silence harmless ``Request was canceled''
messages that Copilot logs whenever a completion request is
superseded (@ref{Suppressing canceled-request noise, , Suppressing canceled-request noise}).
@end itemize

