@node Conditional activation
@section Conditional activation

@findex copilot-extras-enable-conditionally
The function @code{copilot-extras-enable-conditionally} is designed to be
added to a hook such as @code{prog-mode-hook} or @code{text-mode-hook}.  It
activates @samp{copilot-mode} in the current buffer @emph{unless} any of the
following is true:

@enumerate
@item
The buffer is read-only (@code{buffer-read-only} is non-nil).
@item
The buffer's major mode appears in
@code{copilot-extras-excluded-modes} (@ref{@code{copilot-extras-excluded-modes}, , @code{copilot-extras-excluded-modes}}).
@item
The function is called from a non-interactive context (i.e.@comma{}
@code{this-command} is @code{nil})@comma{} such as a timer.  Starting the Copilot
server in such contexts can trigger errors that freeze Emacs.
@item
The buffer is an Org capture buffer (@code{org-capture-mode} is
active).  Copilot's change tracker can crash in these short-lived
buffers.
@end enumerate

This provides a convenient ``enable everywhere except@dots{}'' policy without
requiring per-mode hook configuration.

@node Restarting Copilot
@section Restarting Copilot

@findex copilot-extras-restart-copilot
The function @code{copilot-extras-restart-copilot} quickly disables and
re-enables @samp{copilot-mode} in the current buffer@comma{} with a brief pause
between the two operations.  This is a workaround for situations where
the Copilot process stops providing suggestions.  The function only
acts when @samp{copilot-mode} is already active@comma{} so it is safe to call
unconditionally---for instance@comma{} from a periodic timer.

@node Suppressing canceled-request noise
@section Suppressing canceled-request noise

@vindex copilot-extras-suppressed-error-codes
The user option @code{copilot-extras-suppressed-error-codes} lists JSON-RPC
error codes that should be silenced.  The default value is @samp{(-32800
-32602)}:

@itemize
@item
@samp{-32800} (``Request was canceled''): the server canceled a superseded
request@comma{} which is normal during typing.
@item
@samp{-32602} (``Document for URI could not be found''): a transient URI
mismatch between the editor and the server.
@end itemize

@findex copilot-extras-suppress-canceled-log
The function @code{copilot-extras-suppress-canceled-log} is installed as
@samp{:around} advice on @code{copilot--log}.  It intercepts error-level log
calls whose error object carries a code listed in
@code{copilot-extras-suppressed-error-codes} and silently drops them.  All
other log messages pass through unchanged.

